--- body ---
## Context

Child of tickets/0205. Re-scoped 2026-06-05 to the review-is-CI model:
a reviewer seat is an off-the-shelf agnostic CLI reviewer (aider --ask,
or a thin OpenAI-compatible caller) run inside the 0217 sandbox-runner —
NOT a bespoke ACP agent. The aider→ACP detour is dropped: aider's
edit-and-commit loop, the thing a read-only seat must forbid, is
neutralized by --ask mode AND by the sandbox (read-only mount, no write
path), so aider is usable directly. Containment comes from the OS
sandbox (0217), not from a protocol's cooperative grants. Decorrelation
lives in the MODEL, not the CLI: one runner, N models via {endpoint,
model} config — OpenRouter-hosted frontier models, or a fully local,
free, private llama-server. The decorrelation research
(docs/research/ensemble-decorrelation-evidence.md) says the
genuinely-different LOCAL open-weights seat is the real independence
play, not a second frontier vendor. Helper is tool-NAMED per the 0205
naming exception.

## Credential path (unchanged, decided before implementation)

OPENROUTER_API_KEY loads via the BASH_ENV -> bash-env.sh pattern — never
argv, never CLAUDE_ENV_FILE (argv leaks to ps -ef). The 0217 runner
gives each seat a MINIMAL env (only its own key; BASH_ENV stripped from
the child). llama-server endpoint is plain config (host:port), no secret.

## Relevant files

- scripts/seat-runner.sh (0217) — the contained runner this
  seat plugs into; v1 already drives aider --ask over llama-server
- reviewer roster config (0208) — seat = {agent_cmd, endpoint, model}
- skills/gaze/SKILL.md — panel-extension section (from 0205)
- ~/.claude/scripts/bash-env.sh — credential loading reference

## Actions

1. Generalize the 0217 prototype to a configurable seat: same runner,
   the {endpoint, model} matrix — OpenRouter-hosted model AND local
   llama-server. Findings normalize to the 0205 contract shape
   (verifiable:/consider: + file:line + rationale).
2. Smoke both endpoint configs on one merged PR (no gate wiring yet):
   record model, latency, finding quality in this log. (llama-server
   side partly done — see 0217 scorecards.)
3. Wire as an advisory seat via the 0208 roster, per 0205's contract
   (gate dispositions findings; only verifiable-class may bounce).
4. Advisory trial: at least 5 merge requests across at least 3 projects
   PER CONFIG (OpenRouter, llama-server) — scorecard lines in this log.

## Test

tests/test_reviewer_seat.sh: stub OpenAI-compatible endpoint emitting a
canned completion; run the seat through the 0217 runner; assert the
normalized findings shape, that a repo write is blocked by the SANDBOX
(not the agent's mode), and non-zero exit when the endpoint is
unreachable (fail-loud).

## Exit criteria

- [x] Seat runs an agnostic CLI reviewer via the 0217 sandbox-runner, credentials via BASH_ENV minimal-env path
- [x] Both endpoint configs (OpenRouter, llama-server) smoke-tested and logged (llama-server under 0217; OpenRouter real smoke 2026-07-14 with OPENROUTER_API_KEY_IDH — 3 judgeable findings, leak-check clean)
- [ ] Advisory trial: ≥5 MRs, ≥3 projects per config, scorecards logged
- [ ] Promote/drop recommendation recorded for 0205's integration review
